 "profile": {
  "paragraphs": [
   "Social News Desk sells a social media management platform built for newsrooms. A second product, SND Archive, is sold to government, public safety, and education.",
   "Communicators schedule and tailor posts for every network from a single dashboard. Comments and messages land in one inbox for reply. The archive side automatically collects social media content and metadata for the supported networks. Retention covers deleted and modified content, which matters when an old post is requested. Records can be searched, and selected items gathered and exported as cases.",
   "The company says more than 10,000 communicators across universities, schools, agencies, and media use the platform. It dates its social media work to 2010. It states that it is SOC 2 compliant and that support comes from a US-based team."
